<Base title="About" description="About nth degree">
  <header class="page-header">
    <h1>About</h1>
  </header>

  <div class="content">
    <p>
      I'm <strong>Navish Dadighat</strong> — an engineering leader based in Orange County, CA.
      I've spent over a decade building and scaling engineering teams and platforms at companies
      ranging from startups to the Fortune 100.
    </p>

    <p>
      I currently lead a global engineering organization of 75–100 across the US, Philippines, UK, and India.
      Before that, I led engineering through a $1B acquisition at Ambry Genetics, built teams from scratch,
      and navigated the messy reality of M&A from both sides. I also build agentic AI pipelines, wrangle
      Kubernetes clusters, and still write code when no one's looking.
    </p>

    <h2>About this blog</h2>
    <p>
      nth degree is where I write about what I actually build, break, and fix — infrastructure,
      networking, homelab engineering, and the platform work that underpins it all. No fluff,
      no hot takes. Specifics over generalities.
    </p>

    <p>
      The lab runs on a Proxmox cluster in my garage. Every post here is rooted in something real.
    </p>

